    "message": "perf(ingest): memoize module resolution\n\nResolution runs per bound relationship, and index.ts issues two full lookups\nof the same (source, specifier, kind) triple for each one, so a repo with\npaths/baseUrl pays the walk over and over.\n\nCache on the three things that actually change the answer: the source\ndirectory (which config applies), the source extension (a .js caller prefers\n.js over .ts), and the specifier and kind. Keying on the directory alone —\nthe obvious shortcut — would serve a .js caller's answer to a .ts caller in\nthe same folder and silently flip the preference order, so there is a test\nthat runs both orders and a repeat.\n\nMeasured on a synthetic 2000-file workspace, 1000 calls across 50 source\ndirectories: 24.87us/call -> 3.38us/call, ~7.4x.\n\nix-cli: 941 passed, 1 skipped. typecheck, lint, knip clean.",
